course: dictionary
lesson: 13446
title: Places to stay
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hostel is a cheap place to stay, often with shared rooms and bunk beds. «The school group slept in a hostel by the lake.» The clues are cheap, shared and bunk beds. The children were not in a grand hotel with a room each.
explain: Hostels are for travellers and young people, and sometimes for people with no home or for students. «Maya lived in a hostel while she studied at college.» The clue is studied at college, so a hostel can be a home for a time, not only a holiday stay.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «We stayed in a cheap place with bunk beds on our trip» still makes sense with hostel, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: A hostel is a cheap place to stay, often with shared rooms and bunk beds.
fact: A youth hostel is a hostel for young people and travellers on trips.
fact: Some hostels are buildings where people with no home can sleep for a time.
fact: Students may also live in a hostel while they study.
fact: Useful phrases: «youth hostel» and «stay in a hostel».
exercise: «The school group slept in a hostel by the lake.» What is a hostel? | A kind of hospital for animals | A large shop selling books | *A cheap place to stay, often with bunk beds | A boat used for fishing
exercise: «The youth hostel had a room with beds stacked on top of each other for twelve travellers.» Find and copy one word that describes beds stacked on top of each other. | youth | room | travellers | *bunk
exercise: Jayden says a hostel is only for holidays. Is he right? | Yes, hostels are only for families with cars | No, hostels are only for teachers | *No, students and people with no home can live in one for a time | Yes, hostels are only for holidays
test: «Maya lived in a hostel while she studied at college.» What does this tell you about a hostel? | A shop for sweets | A type of bus | A school for cooking | *A place where a person can live for a time
test: Ella says a youth hostel is a fancy hotel where she gets a room of her own. Is she right? | *No, a youth hostel is cheap and often has shared rooms | No, a hostel is a type of car | Yes, every room is private and very grand | Yes, it is the same as a palace
exam: What is the name for a hostel for young people and travellers on trips? | *Youth hostel | Hostel shop | Youth bus | Youth park
